{
  "id": "forward-pairing",
  "term": "forward pairing",
  "definition": "Forward pairing is a classical conditioning arrangement in which a cue is presented before, and may briefly overlap with, a rewarding stimulus. In the honey bee example in this packet, presenting an odor before sucrose leads the bee to learn the association, so the odor alone can later trigger the proboscis extension response.",
